## ✅ v3.3.0 Released (2026-06-15) — MCP server production release (20 tools)

- **GitHub release v3.3.0 live** (PR #29 dev→main, tag, main CI green). 20-tool MCP server (`mcp_server.py`) promoted to production; no `obs` CLI changes.
- **Version bump** 3.2.3→3.3.0 across 13 files; 2nd hardcoded version assertion found in `__tests__/cli.test.js` (separate dir from `tests/obs.test.js`). Tests: 287 pytest + 67 Jest.
- **Fix:** removed stale pinned Cellar path (`…/3.2.3/…`) in `mcp_server._find_obs_python` — the Homebrew `opt` symlink candidate resolves the active version (no per-release pin).
- **Homebrew tap @ 3.3.0** (tap PR #127): resources **13→40** — full `requirements.lock` closure (mcp + transitive). Derived via `pip install -r requirements.lock --dry-run --report` (lock-faithful), NOT `brew update-python-resources` (resolved un-buildable `attrs==26.1.0`). Added `sniffio` (update-python-resources omits it), `depends_on "rust" => :build` (rpds-py/pydantic-core/cryptography sdists), `depends_on "libyaml"`. Gated by `brew reinstall --build-from-source` (built 6m13s, mcp imports OK, db-init clean) + `brew audit --strict` clean. `obs version` → 3.3.0.
- Auto `homebrew-release.yml` fired on the release event (bumped url+sha w/ 13 resources); superseded by manual PR #127 (resources changed → auto-release insufficient).

---

## ✅ v3.2.3 Released (2026-06-15) — obs search + graph fix + stats fix + test suite expansion

- **`obs search <query>`** — new native CLI command: title search across all vaults; `--vault` / `--limit` / `--json` flags.
- **Graph fix** — `obs analyze` cross-vault edge contamination fixed (link queries now JOIN on notes table to scope to target vault).
- **Stats fix** — `obs stats` now shows internal links and broken links separately: `Links: 56 (635 broken)`.
- **52 MCP unit tests** (`test_mcp_server.py`) — full coverage of all 20 MCP tools + 4 resources; edge cases: unicode, empty inputs, path traversal, server stability.
- **32 E2E dogfood tests** (`tests/e2e/test_e2e_mcp.py`) — real subprocess JSON-RPC; run with `E2E=1`.
- **numpy test fix** — numpy-dependent tests now skip gracefully under system Python (was erroring at collection).
- **Docs updated** — cli-reference, refcard, usage, getting-started, testing/overview, changelog, claude-mcp, CLAUDE.md, .STATUS.
- **Release**: PR #27 dev→main merged, tag `v3.2.3`, GitHub release live.
- **Post-release completion (2026-06-15)**: PR #27's main CI was RED — `--strict-markers` rejected the unregistered `asyncio` marker (CI installs `requirements.txt`, no `pytest-asyncio`). Fixing it unmasked 2 more latent Jest failures (man `.TH` not bumped to 3.2.3; the v3.3.0 `mcp` lock tree broke the 6-core contract test). All three fixed in **PR #28** (dev→main, merged, **main CI green**): register `asyncio` marker, bump man `.TH`→3.2.3, fold `mcp` into the lock contract (`CORE_DEPS` 6→7). **Homebrew tap @ 3.2.3** via tap PR #126 (url+sha256 only; gated by `brew reinstall --build-from-source` + `audit --strict`); `obs version`→3.2.3. **Secrets configured** (APP_ID `2874502` + APP_PRIVATE_KEY from GitHub App "Data-Wise Homebrew Automation"); `homebrew-release.yml` dry run (workflow_dispatch v3.2.3, auto_merge=false) went green end-to-end — App token minted, no-op tap update, no stray PR. Auto-Homebrew CI now armed for v3.3.0.

